{
 "kind": "item",
 "name": "Atakebune",
 "category": "ship",
 "era": "1550-1640",
 "region": "Sengoku and early Edo Japan",
 "_about": "the warship of the warring states and of the Korean war: a broad flat hull carrying a fortress -- a box of planked shields (tatebita) the length of the ship, black-beamed, pierced by two rows of loopholes for the arquebuses and bows and by the ports the oars run out through, a gate in each side; its roof a fighting deck behind a loopholed parapet, and on it the yagura, a castle keep of three white-walled storeys under dark tiled eaves with gilt finials; one square sail of matting on a mast that can be lowered, banners along the parapet. (About 30-45 m: the Atake-maru of 1635 was about 47 m, most were smaller -- estimated from the screens and the Kaiyō records)",
